  "_comment": "Source-only Python ctest registrations run on the build-free required lane (`Enforce version & skill sync`) instead of the required macOS gate. Each entry is the registered command with the interpreter dropped and the source root written as {repo}. test/cmake/source_selftest_lane_tests.cmake labels every entry `source-selftest`; tools/ci/ctest_gate_args.py excludes that label on gate events; `tools/ci/source_selftests.py check` (the source-selftest-lane-contract ctest, on the gate) fails when the two drift. Refresh commands with `python3 tools/ci/source_selftests.py write --build-dir build`; add a test with `--add <name>`. An entry must import only the standard library, read only the checkout, and not carry pr-fast. See docs/guides/test-lanes.md.",
